{"title":"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ruhab wrote the list <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/3/3c3bf2e471547ec648e4f1d10f10e6db24740646.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\text{,} 2\\text{,} 8\\text{,} 7\\text{,}9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"17\" /> and then erased one of the five digits. The sum of the remaining four digits was a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Which number did she erase?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/a/7ba2e8c7c30b5abcdaddd2cdff63e7a5d40eee0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 5 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 8 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 7 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we can find the sum of the numbers before one of the numbers is subtracted:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86a1746551d042533d1fac535d77c0ce0eee9c2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 2 + 8 + 7 + 9 = 7 + 15 + 9 = 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"284\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296fac336caaa4265aa24b6ecbc408a348ad7e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> has a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, Ruhab must have erased a number that had the same remainder because the new sum would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a1cd691e241cf4c9ead4de00c066f157daf3ede.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> was the number that was erased.\n</p><p>The only number in the list that had a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/30263042958b4e7b9b4c392b29ff267514b0994f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\"